  "limitations": [
    "Methodological issues in laboratory studies include subject selection, experimenter bias, context effects, impure signals, generation of harmonics, measurement difficulties, generalizability to real-world situations, uncertainty of temporary vs. clinical significance, and potential issues with early extreme exposures and military subjects.",
    "Methodological issues in field studies include problems with drawing causal inferences from correlational data, self-report bias, confounding differences between populations, respondent difficulty in identifying noise sources, and the rarity of pure low-frequency noise making specific effects difficult to identify."
  ],
